# Frontend (Next.js 15)

- App Router, React 19, TypeScript 5 (strict), Tailwind 4, shadcn/ui (Radix).
- `app/**/page.tsx` are RSC (metadata). Interactive screens live in `features/{chat,documents,settings,auth,inspect}`. Shared shell: `components/` + `components/ui`.
- Server data: TanStack Query. Ephemeral UI state: Zustand (chat stores colocated under `features/chat/stores`). No Redux.
- Talk only to `/api/v1/*`. Types should match backend Pydantic models; do not silently rename fields.
- On logout/login, clear React Query and the chat Zustand store. Do not restore `/chat/:sessionId` from `?next=` (session ids are per user).

## Chat (primary screen)

- Split pane: sessions (collapsible) | chat (min ~440px, never a thin strip) | PDF (collapsible). A citation click reopens the PDF pane.
- Citations in the answer are interactive tags, e.g. `Expense_Policy.pdf (p. 4)`.
- Clicking a citation **must**: open that file in the viewer, jump to `page`, and highlight the snippet when coordinates/text exist.
- Reuse the existing SSE chat parser in `api.ts`. Order: `citations` → `token` → `meta`/`done`. Click citation → `Doc.pdf` page, not line-number contract refs.

## Knowledge base admin

- Table: title, size, pages, access tags, status (`pending|processing|ready|failed`).
- Drag-and-drop upload modal with `access_roles` (`HR`, `Finance`, `General`, …). After M5, show current org name; do not send `organization_id` in the chat body.
- Org-admin `/settings`: plan, usage, SSO, domain. If `BILLING_PROVIDER=dev`, show a **Dev billing** badge — not a live checkout. Employee hitting quota sees a toast, not another org’s usage.
- Poll `GET /documents/{id}/status` until `ready` or `failed`; show `stage` (`parse` → `chunk` → `embed`).
- PDF bytes come from `GET /documents/{id}/raw` (auth + org + ACL). Never use a public bucket URL.

Accessibility: keyboard-focusable citations, readable contrast on highlights. Prefer existing shadcn primitives (dialog, table, select, checkbox, tabs, progress, alert, skeleton) over custom CSS.
